Operational governance ensures that Azure environments remain secure, compliant, reliable, and cost-effective throughout their lifecycle. Rather than focusing only on initial deployment, operational governance establishes ongoing processes that guide daily administration and long-term management.

A governance framework typically includes:

* Operational policies
* Standard operating procedures
* Monitoring and alerting
* Incident management
* Change management
* Security reviews
* Compliance reporting
* Continuous improvement

For example, an enterprise may schedule monthly governance reviews to verify compliance, evaluate operational metrics, and identify areas requiring optimization.

A real-life use case is organizations maintaining consistent operational standards across multiple Azure subscriptions and departments.

A well-defined operational governance framework improves service quality while reducing operational risk.
